ues. Notably well-calibrated: E001 `architecture_claims: +1` cites\n71\t`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md` (which exists\n72\tand corroborates the Dashboard premise); E002 `architecture_claims: 0` with the\n73\trationale that no context file covers Documentation — verified: no such file\n74\texists, so 0 is the rule-correct value. E002 `human_process_gates: -1` is\n75\tjustified by HLR-3's explicit technical-review-before-republication requirement.\n76\tNo arithmetic checked (pipeline-computed).\n77\t\n78\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n79\tE001's ACs are testable and anchored to the audit report's defect list\n80\t(keyboard-only completion per flow with every enumerated defect resolved or\n81\tdispositioned, consistent focus indicators, recorded manual walkthrough,\n82\tregression suite pass). E002 has the rule-mandated docs-authoring technical\n83\treview AC with recorded sign-off (reviewer and date), plus a\n84\tno-contradictory-claims AC. No replacement/rollback or konflux-chain ACs are\n85\trequired (not a replacement; Dashboard already onboarded). No\n86\texternally-controlled precondition is misfiled as an AC — republication is the\n87\tepic's own deliverable. No draft-ID references to sibling epics in either epic\n88\tbody.\n89\t\n90\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n91\tFull strategy scope is covered: the four audited flows' keyboard operability and\n92\tfocus-indicator consistency (E001), and the VPAT plus accessibility statement\n93\tupdate, republication, and technical review (E002). Out-of-scope items\n94\t(screen-reader semantics beyond keyboard fixes, flows outside the four) are\n95\texplicitly excluded in E001's scope, matching the strategy. Strategy-level\n96\tcontext is carried forward: the public-sector renewal dependency appears in\n97\tE002's description; the audit-report-as-external-input risk is captured in the\n98\tsummary's Health Warnings and as an AC input rather than a spurious\n99\tInvestigation. A `docs-authoring` epic is present (Rule 11), which HLR-3\n100\trequires in substance even though the strategy lacks a formal Prerequisites &\n101\tProcess Gates section. No conditional branches to check.\n102\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-921dee872ba4aeed","agent_id":"a87d2f2104fce20be","session_id":"84025926-e088-44a2-8c99-e9522ae1f2f6","uuid":"81a7630b-d236-4672-9e13-75a074cede2b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:00:31.077Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bac33f24b530c128","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
